# Google OAuth 2.0 Client ID (Web application) for browser-side Drive & Sheets access.
# This is the ONLY credential this app needs — there is no client secret, because
# the app uses the Google Identity Services (GIS) browser token flow.
#
# How to obtain it:
#   1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/ and create/select a project.
#   2. APIs & Services > Library: enable "Google Drive API" and "Google Sheets API".
#   3. APIs & Services > OAuth consent screen: configure it (External is fine for testing),
#      and add your Google account as a Test user.
#   4. APIs & Services > Credentials > Create Credentials > OAuth client ID:
#        - Application type: Web application
#        - Authorized JavaScript origins: http://localhost:3000
#   5. Copy the generated Client ID below.
#
# Then copy this file to `.env.local` and restart `npm run dev`.

NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com

# --- Google Picker (required for invited clients / collaborators) ---
# The narrow `drive.file` scope means the app CANNOT auto-discover files that a
# contractor shared with a client. When a client logs in, they use the Google
# Picker to explicitly open the project spreadsheet that was shared with them —
# that grants the app access to just that file. Without these, invited clients
# cannot open their shared project.
#
# How to obtain them (same Google Cloud project as the OAuth client above):
#   1. APIs & Services > Library: enable "Google Picker API".
#   2. APIs & Services > Credentials > Create Credentials > API key. Copy it below.
#      (Recommended: restrict the key to the Picker API and your origins.)
#   3. NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_APP_ID is your Google Cloud *project number* (optional).
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_API_KEY=your-google-api-key
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_APP_ID=your-project-number
